            <h3>Cashback Credit Cards</h3>
            <p>Get a percentage of your money back on everyday purchases like groceries, fuel, and dining.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-type">
            <h3>Travel Credit Cards</h3>
            <p>Enjoy travel perks such as free lounge access, air miles, and travel insurance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-type">
            <h3>Low-Interest Credit Cards</h3>
            <p>Save on interest with cards that offer low APR rates, ideal for carrying a balance.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card-type">
            <h3>Premium Credit Cards</h3>
            <p>Experience luxury with cards that offer exclusive benefits like concierge services, special discounts, and more.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section id="apply" class="container">
    <h2>How to Apply for a Credit Card</h2>
    <p style="color: black;">Choosing the right credit card can be overwhelming, but we are here to help. Consider the following factors to find the perfect card:</p>
    <ol>
        <li>Spending Habits:Look at where you spend the most and choose a card that offers rewards or cashback in those categories.</li>
        <li>Annual Fees: Some cards come with annual fees, but the benefits may outweigh the cost. Decide if the perks justify the fee.</li>
        <li>Interest Rates: If you plan to carry a balance, choose a card with a low-interest rate to save on interest charges.</li>
        <li>Rewards and Benefits: Compare the rewards and benefits each card offers and pick one that aligns with your preferences.</li>
    </ol>
</section>
<section id="benefits" class="container">
  <h2>How to Apply for a Credit Card</h2>
  <p style="color: black;">Applying for a credit card with RupeeXpert is simple and quick:</p>
  <ul>
      <li><strong>Compare Cards:</strong>Browse through our selection of credit cards and compare their features and benefits.</li>
      <li><strong>Check Eligibility:</strong> Use our eligibility checker to see which cards you qualify for.</li>
      <li><strong>Apply Online:</strong> Fill out a secure online application form with your personal and financial details.</li>
      <li><strong>Get Approved:</strong> Once your application is approved, you will receive your new credit card and can start enjoying its benefits.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="container">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
    <div class="faq-section">
        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What documents do I need to apply for a credit card?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">You will typically need proof of identity (like a passport or driver's license), proof of address (like a utility bill), and proof of income (like a salary slip or bank statement).</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How long does it take to get approved for a credit card?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Approval times vary by bank, but it usually takes a few days to a week to get approved.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I apply for more than one credit card?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes, you can apply for multiple credit cards, but it's important to manage them responsibly to avoid debt.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I check the status of my credit card application?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">You can check the status of your application by logging into your RupeeXpert account or contacting the bank directly.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What should I do if my credit card application is denied?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">If your application is denied, review the reason provided by the bank, improve your credit score if needed, and consider applying for a different card that better matches your profile.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach(question => {
